/// screen it is on** (`fitWindowToContent`, R1 review): the countdown
/// numeral grows the card 88 pt DOWNWARD — 130 with a note under it — from
/// a fixed top edge, and a panel parked at the bottom of a display, the
/// natural place for a recorder, used to put its Cancel button under the
/// Dock.
///
/// **Visibility during a recording** (decision 7, R2c): the panel orders
/// OUT at `recordingDidStart` for every source but Microphone Only and
/// Camera (below), and the status item is the
/// recording's whole chrome — Pause, Resume and Stop are its menu; File ▸
/// Stop Recording still stops. R1 kept a DISPLAY recording's panel up, its
/// filter excluding Frame Job (R0 q3), and hid only a PICKED window's; the
/// user asked for the dialog to go away whatever is recorded, and a panel
/// whose one live control was a Stop the menu bar also has earned nothing
/// on screen. It comes back after the landing ONLY when it was on screen
/// as the recording began (`showWhenLanded`, read at `recordingDidStart`)
/// AND the landing left a note (`revealIfNoted`, `+Landing.swift`): a stop
/// from the system's own indicator, a closed target, a microphone problem,
/// a refused resume, a failure. A clean recording lands and the panel
/// stays away, and a panel closed before the recording began stays closed
/// whatever the note; ⌥⌘N shows it again. `show()` BEEPS while
/// `hiddenForRecording` (R1 review) — the welcome window's button reaches
/// it — because a panel un-hidden into the recording would be in the file;
/// the quit guard goes through `revealControls()` instead (`+Pause.swift`).
/// **It takes key only from an active Frame Job** (spec §11, #137): shown from
/// the background it is ordered front without key, so Return stays with
/// the app in front. **A voice-over stays UP** (#99): nothing is filmed, so
/// the rows lock, the meter stays live, Record reads Stop with a Pause /
/// Resume button beside it; Close takes the panel away and the recording
/// carries on — the welcome button and the quit guard show the panel again,
/// and ⌥⌘N (File ▸ Stop Recording) and the status item stop it. **So does
/// a camera recording** (CAM-5), on the same terms: nothing on screen is
/// filmed.
///
/// Two limits of that chrome, accepted (R2 review). With the panel hidden
/// the status item is the ONLY Pause and Resume, and macOS drops a status
/// item that does not fit the menu bar — behind a notch, in a crowded bar
/// — so there Stop survives in the File menu and Pause and Resume do not.
/// And "●" and "❚❚" differ in width under `variableLength`, so the items to
/// the left of it shift by a few points at each pause and resume.
///
/// **Quit while recording, and the order AppKit asks in.**
/// `AppDelegate.applicationShouldTerminate` cancels a quit while
/// `ScreenRecorder.shared.isRecording` and calls `revealControls()` — the
/// status item's menu, opened, while this panel is hidden for its
/// recording; `show()` for any other (a tool's, which File ▸ Stop Recording
/// ends) — and it is a BACKSTOP: `NSDocumentController` reviews modified
/// documents FIRST, so the save sheet comes before the guard, and a target
/// document the review CLOSED lands as `.newProject` —
/// `RecordingLanding.resolve` looks the destination up by `recipeKey`,
/// never minted twice, so the miss is exact, and the landing's note says
/// the document was closed.
///
/// **Two Record Into rules.** The popup is built from `NSMenuItem`s carrying
/// each document's `recipeKey` in `representedObject` and is read from
/// `selectedItem`, never by index: `NSPopUpButton.addItem(withTitle:)`
/// REMOVES a same-titled row (phase 4's defect), and two untitled documents
/// read alike. And it follows the FRONT document until the person chooses a
/// row themselves (`chosenDestination`), re-synced by a one-second timer
/// while the panel is visible — rows compared before any rebuild, so a menu
/// the person has open is never rebuilt under the pointer — **and only while
/// the phase is idle** (`rebuildDestinations`, R1 review): from the press
/// of Record to the landing the rows are FROZEN at what the person saw when
/// they pressed it, whichever document comes to the front meanwhile, and
/// `landed()`'s own rebuild is what moves them again. The destination the
/// recording actually lands in was captured from the controls at the
/// countdown's end and cannot move either way; what the freeze buys is that
/// the row on screen and the destination in the choice agree.
///
/// Every choice persists under a `FrameJobRecording…` key (written on change,
/// read on show); the harness pins all eighteen on `FrameJobExportChoice`'s terms.
/// `.picked` is the one source that cannot persist — a filter is not a
/// value — so a reopened panel with a picked window keeps the row only while
/// the filter is still held; Microphone Only and Camera persist for the
/// session only (the camera itself is remembered, the row is not). "Record
/// the camera too" (CAM-11) is remembered across launches, and so is Record
/// shortcuts (road map creator-jobs CU6, spec §11 CU-62), off by default, and
/// Cursor (CU3c, spec §11 CU-36), whose `""` follows the source's default,
/// the three "When it lands:" boxes (CU10, spec §11 CU-102), on, on and off
/// when never set, and the camera's Layout and cutout (CO-82), Corner and off.
final class RecorderPanelController: NSWindowController {
    static let shared = RecorderPanelController()

    // MARK: - Defaults keys

    static let displayKey = "FrameJobRecordingDisplay"
    static let microphoneKey = "FrameJobRecordingMicrophone"
    static let systemAudioKey = "FrameJobRecordingSystemAudio"
    static let showClicksKey = "FrameJobRecordingShowClicks"
    static let rateKey = "FrameJobRecordingRate"
    static let sizeKey = "FrameJobRecordingSize"
    static let includeFrameJobWindowsKey = "FrameJobRecordingIncludeFrameJobWindows"
    static let cameraKey = "FrameJobRecordingCamera"
    static let cameraFormatKey = "FrameJobRecordingCameraFormat"
    /// "Record the camera too" (spec §11 CAM-11 (2)); an absent key reads as off.
    static let cameraBesideKey = "FrameJobRecordingCameraBeside"
    /// "Enhance the microphone when it lands" (spec §11 AU-69); an absent key reads as off.
    static let enhanceMicrophoneKey = "FrameJobRecordingEnhanceMicrophone"
    /// Record shortcuts (spec §11 CU-62); an absent key reads as off.
    static let keysKey = "FrameJobRecordingKeys"
    /// Cursor (spec §11 CU-36 (d)): `""` follows the source, else a `RecordingCursor` raw value.
    static let cursorKey = "FrameJobRecordingCursor"

    // MARK: - Metrics and vocabulary

    /// Wider than `sheetWidth`: the microphone row is a popup AND a 120 pt
    /// meter beside the 106 pt label column, which 420 cannot hold.
    static let cardWidth: CGFloat = 500
    static let controlWidth: CGFloat = 200
    /// The Source popup's last row, "Window…", by tag; display rows carry
    /// their `CGDirectDisplayID` in `representedObject`.
    static let windowTag = 1
    static let countdownSeconds = 3
    static let rates = [30, 60]
    /// The note under Record shortcuts (spec §11 CU-60, CU-62).
    static let recordShortcutsSentence =
        "Records each shortcut you press with ⌘ or ⌃, or ⌥ with an arrow, Delete, Return, Tab "
        + "or Esc, and when you type, never what you type. Nothing is recorded while an app "
        + "holds secure input."

    /// Where the panel is in a recording's life. `syncPhase()` draws it.
    enum Phase: Equatable {
        case idle
        case countdown(Int)
        case starting
        case recording
        case paused
        case stopping
        case landing
    }

    var phase: Phase = .idle {
        didSet { syncPhase() }
    }

    let recorder = ScreenRecorder.shared

    // The controls — internal rather than private because the recording flow
    // lives in an extension in another file, and `private` does not cross one.
    let sourcePopup = NSPopUpButton(frame: .zero, pullsDown: false)
    let includeFrameJobCheckbox = NSButton(
        checkboxWithTitle: "Include Frame Job windows", target: nil, action: nil)
    let cameraBesideCheckbox = NSButton(
        checkboxWithTitle: "Record the camera too", target: nil, action: nil)
    let cameraPopup = NSPopUpButton(frame: .zero, pullsDown: false)
    let formatPopup = NSPopUpButton(frame: .zero, pullsDown: false)
    let microphonePopup = NSPopUpButton(frame: .zero, pullsDown: false)
    let enhanceMicrophoneCheckbox = NSButton(
        checkboxWithTitle: "Enhance the microphone when it lands", target: nil, action: nil)
    let meterView = LevelMeterView(meter: ScreenRecorder.shared.meter)
    let systemAudioSwitch = NSSwitch()
    let showClicksSwitch = NSSwitch()
    /// Cursor (spec §11 CU-36): "Separate", "In the picture"; each item's
    /// `representedObject` its `RecordingCursor` raw value.
    let cursorPopup = NSPopUpButton(frame: .zero, pullsDown: false)
    let recordShortcutsCheckbox = NSButton(
        checkboxWithTitle: "Record shortcuts", target: nil, action: nil)
    let recordShortcutsNote = NSTextField(wrappingLabelWithString: "")
    /// "When it lands:" (spec §11 CU-102 (a), `+Polish.swift`).
    let polishBoxes = RecorderPolishBoxes()
    /// The camera's Layout and Remove-background box (spec §11 CO-82, `+CameraLanding.swift`).
    let cameraLanding = RecorderCameraLandingControls()
    let ratePopup = NSPopUpButton(frame: .zero, pullsDown: false)
    let sizePopup = NSPopUpButton(frame: .zero, pullsDown: false)
    let sizeNote = NSTextField(labelWithString: "")
    let destinationPopup = NSPopUpButton(frame: .zero, pullsDown: false)
    let countdownLabel = NSTextField(labelWithString: "")
    let noteLabel = NSTextField(wrappingLabelWithString: "")
    let statusLabel = NSTextField(labelWithString: "")
    let recordButton = AccentButton(
        title: "Record", symbol: "record.circle", fallback: "●",
        tooltip: "Start recording after a three-second countdown",
        action: #selector(record(_:)), fill: DS.meterClip)
    let closeButton = StickerButton(
        title: "Close", style: .secondary, target: nil, action: #selector(closePanel(_:)))
    let voiceOverPauseButton = StickerButton(
        title: "Pause", style: .secondary, target: nil, action: #selector(pauseButtonPressed(_:)))
    let cameraPreview = CameraPreviewWell()
    let card: NSView

    /// The picker's filter, held while the Source popup shows "Window
    /// (picked)". Cleared when a display row is chosen.
    var pickedFilter: SCContentFilter?
    var pickerObserved = false
    /// The Source row to fall back to when the picker is cancelled.
    var sourceBeforePick = 0
    /// nil follows the front document; set by the popup's own action.
    var chosenDestination: RecordingDestination?
    /// nil follows the source's default (CU-36 (d)); set only by the Cursor popup's own change.
    var cursorChosen: RecordingCursor? = nil
    /// A recording is running and the panel is off screen for it (`show()`
    /// beeps). Set at EVERY `recordingDidStart`, visible panel or not;
    /// `showWhenLanded` remembers whether it WAS visible, which is what
    /// `revealIfNoted` reads after the landing.
    var hiddenForRecording = false
    var showWhenLanded = false
    /// From `panelWillClose`'s first line until `show()`: the preview's
    /// step reads the panel as not visible, so a close never builds a capture.
    var panelClosing = false
    /// `AVCaptureDevice`'s two observers while the panel is up (`+Devices.swift`).
    var deviceObservers: [NSObjectProtocol] = []
    /// A device list may have changed (a notification, or observers newly added)
    /// and is not yet applied.
    var devicesPending = false
    /// The recorder's sentence for a resume it refused (`+Pause.swift`):
    /// REPLACED by each retry, cleared when a resume lands or the next
    /// countdown begins, one of the two parts the live note is rebuilt
    /// from, and a sentence the landing's note carries (`+Landing.swift`).
    var resumeProblem: String?
    /// Each press of Record is one attempt, numbered, and the completions
    /// the attempt hands out carry its number (`+Recording.swift`): a
    /// shareable-content answer from an attempt that was abandoned or timed
    /// out is told apart by it and ignored.
    var startGeneration = 0
    /// The current attempt has reached `ScreenRecorder.start` — from here
    /// the recorder's own arm ceiling is the bound and a Stop goes through
    /// `stop()`; before it, the lookup is the panel's to abandon.
    var launched = false
    var countdownTimer: Timer?
    var startTimer: Timer?
    var tickTimer: Timer?
    var landingTimer: Timer?
    var syncTimer: Timer?
    var landingAttempts = 0
    var statusItem: RecorderStatusItem?

    private init() {
        let panel = NSPanel(
            contentRect: NSRect(x: 0, y: 0, width: Self.cardWidth, height: 360),
            styleMask: [.titled, .closable, .nonactivatingPanel],
            backing: .buffered,
            defer: false)
        panel.title = "New Recording"
        panel.level = .floating
        // See the type doc: `NSPanel` defaults this to TRUE.
        panel.hidesOnDeactivate = false
        panel.isExcludedFromWindowsMenu = true
        panel.isReleasedWhenClosed = false
        panel.backgroundColor = DS.chromeBackground

        let content = NSStackView()
        card = makeSheetView(
            hint: "The recording is saved as a movie in the Frame Job Recordings folder and "
                + "added to the project you choose at the playhead, or opened as a new "
                + "project at the rate you pick.",
            content: content,
            buttonRow: makeButtonRow(
                cancel: closeButton, apply: recordButton, secondary: voiceOverPauseButton,
                leading: [statusLabel]),
            width: Self.cardWidth)
        super.init(window: panel)

        buildRows(into: content)
        // The card is a subview pinned at the top-left of a plain root, and
        // the window is sized to the card's fitting size by
        // `fitWindowToContent()` — never the window's content view itself,
        // whose autoresizing constraints would fight the card's own width and
        // vertical chain whenever a label appears or disappears.
        let root = NSView()
        root.wantsLayer = true
        card.translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints = false
        root.addSubview(card)
        NSLayoutConstraint.activate([
            card.topAnchor.constraint(equalTo: root.topAnchor),
            card.leadingAnchor.constraint(equalTo: root.leadingAnchor),
        ])
        panel.contentView = root
        recordButton.target = self
        closeButton.target = self
        voiceOverPauseButton.target = self

        rebuildSources()
        rebuildMicrophones()
        rebuildCameras()
        rebuildDestinations()
        restoreChoices()
        refreshSizeNote()
        syncPhase()
        panel.center()

        NotificationCenter.default.addObserver(
            self, selector: #selector(panelWillClose(_:)),
            name: NSWindow.willCloseNotification, object: panel)
    }

    @available(*, unavailable)
    required init?(coder: NSCoder) {
        fatalError("RecorderPanelController does not support NSCoder")
    }

    // MARK: - Actions

    @objc func controlChanged(_ sender: Any?) {
        if let sender = sender as? NSPopUpButton, sender === sourcePopup {
            if sender.selectedItem?.tag == Self.windowTag {
                presentPicker()
            } else {
                pickedFilter = nil
                sourcePopup.menu?.item(withTag: Self.windowTag)?.title = "Window…"
            }
        }
        if let sender = sender as? NSPopUpButton, sender === destinationPopup {
            chosenDestination = currentChoice().destination
        }
        if let sender = sender as? NSPopUpButton, sender === cameraPopup { rebuildCameraFormats() }
        if let sender = sender as? NSPopUpButton, sender === cursorPopup {
            cursorChosen = RecordingCursor(
                rawValue: cursorPopup.selectedItem?.representedObject as? String ?? "")
        }
        persistChoices()
        refreshSizeNote()
        syncControlsEnabled()
        syncCameraPreview()
    }

    @objc private func closePanel(_ sender: Any?) {
        window?.close()
    }

    /// A countdown must not go on in a panel nobody can see: closing cancels
    /// it, and a microphone or camera the countdown prepared is let go with it — said
    /// again here rather than left to `cancelCountdown`, because a panel
    /// closed during the microphone PROMPT (before any countdown) may also
    /// hold one, and an input left open past the panel is the leak the
    /// discard exists to close (R1 review). A close while `.starting` is a
    /// Stop (R2 review) — the attempt abandoned before `launch`, the
    /// recording stopped after it, `stopRecording`'s own two arms — because
    /// a start that ran on behind a closed panel would read `showWhenLanded`
    /// false and land every later note where nobody sees it. A RECORDING
    /// carries on — the status item and File ▸ Stop Recording can end it —
    /// and the sync timer stops until the next `show()`. `panelClosing` is
    /// set FIRST, so the phase change below steps the preview to off and
    /// never builds a capture (CAM-7 (5)), the device observers go (CAM-8 (1)),
    /// and the well is emptied last.
    @objc private func panelWillClose(_ note: Notification) {
        panelClosing = true
        switch phase {
        case .countdown: cancelCountdown()
        case .starting: stopRecording()
        default: break
        }
        recorder.discardPreparedMicrophone()
        recorder.discardPreparedCamera()
        stopObservingDevices()
        syncTimer?.invalidate()
        syncTimer = nil
        cameraPreview.showMessage(nil)
    }
}

import AppKit

/// File ▸ New Recording… (⌥⌘N) and the welcome window's third button —
/// road map 3, R1c. Two `@objc` actions and nothing stored, on purpose:
/// `AppDelegate` has no stored properties, and the chrome probes
/// (`phase6_chrome.py`, `phase9_probe.py`) instantiate `AppDelegate()` to
/// build the menu bar, so anything stored here would be built in every one
/// of them. The panel is `RecorderPanelController.shared` — one instance for
/// the life of the process, `ExportQueueWindowController`'s mould — because it
/// outlives documents and must exist with none open, and the recorder is
/// `ScreenRecorder.shared`.
///
/// It is a nil-target action, `newProject`'s shape (`AppDelegate.swift`): the
/// item resolves down the responder chain to the application delegate, which
/// is what lets it work from the welcome window and from a document window
/// alike. While a recording runs — PAUSED included: `isRecording` is every
/// state past idle — the same item reads "Stop Recording"
/// (`AppDelegate.validateMenuItem` retitles it from `ScreenRecorder.shared`),
/// and this action then stops instead of showing. File ▸ Pause Recording
/// (#98), directly under it with no key, pauses and resumes: retitled
/// Resume Recording from the recorder's state, live only while a recording
/// runs, and routed as the Stop is below — a second door beside the status
/// item's rows (R2c), for a person who looks in the File menu first.
///
/// **Whose recording it is decides the route** (R1 review). The retitle reads
/// the RECORDER, which is one object shared by the panel and the
/// `record_screen` tool, so "Stop Recording" also shows over a recording the
/// tool started — and the panel's `stopRecording()` rightly beeps at one that
/// is not its own, which left the menu item a beep. So: the panel's own
/// recording (its phase `.recording`, `.paused` or `.starting`) stops through
/// the panel, which lands it exactly as its Stop button would; anything else
/// the recorder holds stops through `ScreenRecorder.shared.stop()` with no
/// completion, and the session's `onFinish` — the tool's — lands it; and
/// with nothing recording the panel is shown. Pause Recording takes the
/// same route: the panel's `.recording` / `.paused` through its own
/// `pauseRecording()` / `resumeRecording()`, anything else through the
/// recorder's `pause()` / `resume()`, whose refusal beeps.
///
/// **The welcome button has its own action** (R2 review). It used to send
/// `newRecording`, whose first arm is the Stop above — but the button's
/// title never changes, so a press during a recording stopped it under a
/// label that said "New Recording…". `showRecorderPanel` only shows: during
/// a recording that is a beep (`show()` while `hiddenForRecording`), which
/// is what an un-retitled button can honestly do. The look and the title
/// are untouched, since a chrome proof photographs the welcome window.
extension AppDelegate {
    @objc func newRecording(_ sender: Any?) {
        let panel = RecorderPanelController.shared
        switch panel.phase {
        case .recording, .paused, .starting:
            panel.stopRecording()
        default:
            if ScreenRecorder.shared.isRecording {
                ScreenRecorder.shared.stop()
            } else {
                panel.show()
            }
        }
    }

    /// File ▸ Pause Recording / Resume Recording (the header). A tool's
    /// status item flips at once, on the recorder's
    /// `pauseDidChangeNotification` (#181).
    @objc func pauseOrResumeRecording(_ sender: Any?) {
        let panel = RecorderPanelController.shared
        switch panel.phase {
        case .recording:
            panel.pauseRecording()
        case .paused:
            panel.resumeRecording()
        default:
            let recorder = ScreenRecorder.shared
            do {
                if recorder.isPaused { try recorder.resume() } else { try recorder.pause() }
            } catch {
                NSSound.beep()
            }
        }
    }

    /// The welcome window's New Recording… button (the header): the panel
    /// shown, or a beep while a recording has it hidden.
    @objc func showRecorderPanel(_ sender: Any?) {
        RecorderPanelController.shared.show()
    }
}
